WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.443 --> 00:00:02.348
- [Ari] If you're thinking
of a wild mushroom,

00:00:02.348 --> 00:00:04.613
you're probably thinking of death

00:00:04.613 --> 00:00:06.750
and poisoning and vomiting.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.531
- [Jenna] But, now that
I'm a mushroom hunter,

00:00:08.531 --> 00:00:10.912
I think wonder.
- [Ari] Opportunity.

00:00:10.912 --> 00:00:12.850
- [Jenna] Delicacy.
- [Ari] Potential.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:13.898
- [Woman] Beauty.

00:00:13.898 --> 00:00:15.181
- [Man] Every corner in the forest

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:18.976
has a new surprise in the
mycological world behind it.

00:00:18.976 --> 00:00:20.333
My name is Ari Rockland-Miller.

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:22.260
- [Woman] And I'm Jenna Antonino DiMare.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.254
- [Ari] And we are mycophiles.

00:00:23.254 --> 00:00:25.505
- [Jenna] AKA, mushroom lovers.

00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:29.012
(easygoing instrumental music)

00:00:29.012 --> 00:00:31.951
- In the United States
alone, there are at least

00:00:31.951 --> 00:00:35.606
40 or 50 gourmet edible wild mushrooms,

00:00:35.606 --> 00:00:38.200
and those run the gamut
from the chanterelle

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.783
with a powerful apricot aroma,

00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:43.898
to the black trumpet with
an earthy fig-like flavor

00:00:43.898 --> 00:00:46.887
to hen of the woods, which
looks like a hen roosting

00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:48.827
at the base of an oak tree in the fall.

00:00:48.827 --> 00:00:51.660
There's an unbelievable diversity.

00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:55.912
When I was a little kid,
I would just pile up

00:00:55.912 --> 00:00:58.326
every mushroom I could find
in the woods around my house.

00:00:58.326 --> 00:01:00.938
That was the beginning of the journey.

00:01:00.938 --> 00:01:03.363
I do have dreams about wild mushrooms,

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.600
and then I sort of wake up.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.553
And the first thing I want
to do the next morning

00:01:06.553 --> 00:01:08.307
is get out for mushrooms.

00:01:08.307 --> 00:01:11.974
(lively instrumental music)

00:01:18.027 --> 00:01:19.588
Often, I'm moving fast,

00:01:19.588 --> 00:01:22.365
looking for brightly colored mushrooms.

00:01:22.365 --> 00:01:24.851
Other times, I'm really getting
down on my hands and knees

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:27.263
crawling around the moss
at the base of a beech tree

00:01:27.263 --> 00:01:29.563
looking for a black trumpet.

00:01:29.563 --> 00:01:32.032
- Ari can become extremely enthusiastic

00:01:32.032 --> 00:01:33.421
about hunting for mushrooms.

00:01:33.421 --> 00:01:35.743
And there have been times in the past

00:01:35.743 --> 00:01:37.913
where he'll be out for
hours and hours and hours

00:01:37.913 --> 00:01:41.712
at a time but won't
come back with anything.

00:01:41.712 --> 00:01:43.486
- Finding them does take time,

00:01:43.486 --> 00:01:45.871
but every now and then, all
of a sudden, you see one.

00:01:45.871 --> 00:01:49.538
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.529
And that is the most powerful reverie,

00:01:53.529 --> 00:01:55.946
unbelievable rush every time.

00:02:00.396 --> 00:02:02.333
We use our knife and our mushroom brush,

00:02:02.333 --> 00:02:04.474
and fill up our basket.

00:02:04.474 --> 00:02:05.925
- [Jenna] We don't over-harvest mushrooms.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:09.124
There isn't a monetary incentive.

00:02:09.124 --> 00:02:10.659
- [Ari] We do want to
leave some in the ground

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:13.992
to spread their spores and to reproduce.

00:02:17.038 --> 00:02:19.081
The hunt is intrinsically satisfying.

00:02:19.081 --> 00:02:20.770
It's an epic treasure hunt.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:25.318
It reconnects me to a
childhood sense of wonder.

00:02:25.318 --> 00:02:27.547
On a good day, we can bring home

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.047
many pounds of wild mushrooms.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.968
- [Jenna] When we bring
our mushrooms back,

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:41.011
it's always such a joy to look
through our find from the day

00:02:41.011 --> 00:02:43.478
and cook them up that evening.

00:02:43.478 --> 00:02:47.395
(easygoing instrumental music)

00:02:51.343 --> 00:02:54.251
We don't resell the mushrooms
that we find in the forest.

00:02:54.251 --> 00:02:56.395
We instead enjoy them ourselves.

00:02:56.395 --> 00:03:00.562
We pick just enough to share
with our family and friends.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.194
- [Ari] Mushrooms have taught me

00:03:03.194 --> 00:03:05.404
that even in the tiniest things,

00:03:05.404 --> 00:03:08.552
there's so much potential
that there are whole worlds

00:03:08.552 --> 00:03:12.840
that we ignore that
contain so much flavor,

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.840
beauty, mystery, wonder.

